        "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">A</span> Strike</p><hr /><p><em>A corked flask of oily, black-green liquid that clings to the glass in slow, dripping strands, with a bitter, acrid smell.</em></p><p>The bomb deals 4d6 poison damage and 4 poison splash damage.</p><p><strong>Field Benefit</strong> The Toxicologist research field's benefit of interchanging acid and poison damage still applies to this vial. Applying the vial to your own weapon or ammunition as a single action also uses the Toxicologist's field benefit.</p><p><strong>Applied</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">A</span> Interact. Apply the vial as an injury poison to a weapon you're holding, or to a piece of ammunition on your person or loaded in a weapon you're holding. The vial is used up, and the weapon or ammunition gains one of these effects:</p><ul><li>@UUID[Compendium.marquiste-additions.corpsecaps-cauldron.Item.2642lr60GwHb75yY]{Toxic Coating} The vial's initial damage is added to the first successful Strike with the coated weapon or ammunition.</li><li>@UUID[Compendium.marquiste-additions.corpsecaps-cauldron.Item.RDgt9nkXHhA2QEi4]{Advanced Toxic Coating} (Advanced Vial, 11th level) As Toxic Coating, and the creature also takes persistent poison damage equal to the vial's splash damage.</li></ul><p><strong>Special</strong> If your previous action was to create this vial with Quick Alchemy, applying it to a weapon you're holding, or to ammunition on your person or loaded in a weapon you're holding, costs no action. This is a feature of the Toxicologist's Field Benefit.</p>"
